# Advertising ethics — no dumps, no cheating

Paid Search, RSA, sitelinks, and cert-home copy that ads land on must describe **legitimate exam prep** only.

## Do not

- Bid on dump, brain dump, exam dump, cheat, cheat sheet, actual exam, real exam questions, pass guaranteed, VCE/ETE dump-player, or torrent intent.
- Build or re-enable a dump-intercept / dump-alternative campaign.
- Claim questions come from PDFs, forums, study groups, or dump answer keys.
- Use dump, braindump, or “not a dump” in RSA, display paths, or ad descriptions.

## Do

- Add those terms as **campaign negatives** (Launch 40 and any CCNA/ENCOR Search campaign).
- Lead with verified, blueprint-tagged practice, timed simulation, and official-source keys (CompTIA, Cisco, NIST, RFCs).
- If dump/cheat queries appear in Search terms, negate immediately. Do not add them as positives.

